every GPU backend's device discovery stalled past the deadline dies by SIGALRM within it, with the diagnostic naming the backend and the bound: true
opening a device, and reading the properties or limits, are guarded the same way: true
a deadline of one microsecond, which can expire before arming returns, still reads as the deadline: SIGALRM with the diagnostic: true
with device_init_deadline=0 a stall three times the deadline above runs out and the process exits normally: true
under the program's own SIGALRM handler no deadline is armed: the stall runs out, the handler never runs and is still installed: true
the program's own handler and its own 0.3 s timer: the handler runs once, on time, during the stall, and is still installed after it: true
a pending 1 s timer under the default disposition fires on time during a 3 s stall, killing the process by SIGALRM without the deadline's diagnostic: true
after a guarded call returns, SIGALRM has its default disposition again, the timer is idle, and the process outlives the deadline: true
a guarded entry point stays guarded after a call that returned: a later stall in it dies by the deadline: true
with SIGALRM blocked in the process's only OCaml thread, the deadline still fires: true
a blocked SIGALRM already pending does not hide the deadline: its diagnostic is written, and the process dies by SIGALRM: true
a SIGALRM sent or raised by anything else during a region meets the program's own disposition: the default action kills, and nothing of the deadline's is written: true
a real-time timer the program starts during a region is left in place: it fires on time after the region, killing by SIGALRM without the deadline's diagnostic: true
with fd 2 a full pipe nobody reads, the deadline still kills the process by SIGALRM, its backstop alarm firing while the diagnostic's write is blocked: true
the backstop's 2 s are measured, not counted in naps: with the process's timers throttled so every nap oversleeps by far (as on a loaded macOS VM), the full-pipe case still dies by SIGALRM within 10 s of the stall's start: true
a child forked from inside an armed region gets a deadline of its own: its stall dies by SIGALRM, and the parent's region returns: true
a region a fork child inherited, returning after a new domain of the child armed its own, leaves that deadline armed: the domain's wedged stall still kills the child by SIGALRM with the diagnostic (gh-ocannl-1446): true
guarded regions are serialized: a wedged one entered while a healthy one held the timer is still killed by its own deadline after the healthy one returns: true
a SIGALRM an ancestor caught with SA_SIGINFO reaches an exec'd process as its default disposition, and the deadline is armed there (on macOS the flag survives the exec): true
the cc backends' entry points are not guarded: the stall hook never runs: true
tools/test-run.sh's digest reads the diagnostic's tag as it is written: true
